<title>HONG KONG: Public Bank mandates HK$1.0 bln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Public Bank mandates HK$1.0 bln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's Public Bank has mandated five banks to arrange a three-year HK$1.0 billion floating rate certificates of deposit issue, arranger Sanwa International Finance said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Government approval still is pending.</p>
<p>The other arrangers are Chase Manhattan Asia, HSBC Markets, Standard Chartered Bank and Tokyo-Mitsubishi International Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used for general funding requirements.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
